  "benefits_features_and_faqs": {
    "about_overview": "Cardholders can earn up to 28 SC Points for every Rs. 200 spent on SpiceJet , along with 2X rewards (12 SC Points per Rs. 200) on day-to-day spends , including online bill payments, online food ordering, and online entertainment. The accumulated reward points can be redeemed against SpiceJet flight tickets, meal vouchers, etc., via SpiceJet mobile app or website. The card also compensates for its joining fee of Rs. 2,000 by offering a flight ticket voucher worth Rs. 4,000 along with complimentary SpiceClub Gold Membership. However, one important point to note is that despite being a travel credit card, it does not offer international lounge visits and charges a high forex markup fee of 3.5%. Also, the domestic lounge visits are spend-based , which limits the card’s overall value. This card is a suitable option for consumers who frequently travel and prefer to make bookings via SpiceJet.",
